  <section id="mechanism" class="briefing-slide tone-gold" aria-labelledby="mechanism-title">
    <div class="slide-inner taskvector-slide taskvector-method-slide">
      <h2 id="mechanism-title">{t('参数确实在变，但它们到底朝哪里变？', 'The parameters are changing, but which way are they moving?')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('TaskVector 可以理解成一支“参数方向箭头”：把一次学习前后的参数相减，就能看参数移动了多少、连续更新是否同向，以及拿掉这段参数变化后行为会不会跟着变。它只负责诊断参数变化，最终 WebShop 成绩仍由冻结终评回答。', 'Think of a TaskVector as a parameter-direction arrow: subtract parameters before and after learning to measure how far they moved, whether successive updates align, and whether behavior changes when that accumulated change is removed. It is a diagnostic; the frozen final still determines WebShop performance.')}</p>
      <div class="taskvector-equation" aria-label={t('TaskVector 定义', 'TaskVector definition')}>
        <span>TaskVector</span>
        <strong>v = θ<sub>after</sub> − θ<sub>before</sub></strong>
        <p>{t('θ 是模型参数；v 是这一次学习真正走过的参数方向。', 'θ denotes model parameters; v is the parameter direction taken by this learning step.')}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="taskvector-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><strong>{t('看移动多少', 'measure distance')}</strong><p>{t('‖v‖ 看参数移动的大小。', '‖v‖ measures how far the parameters moved.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><strong>{t('看方向是否一致', 'compare direction')}</strong><p>{t('方向相似度（cosine）看相邻两次更新是在顺着前一次继续走，还是开始往不同方向拉。', 'Cosine shows whether adjacent updates continue in a similar direction or begin pulling apart.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><strong>{t('看行为会不会变', 'test behavior')}</strong><p>{t('拿掉累计 SD-LoRA 参数变化后，固定 24 个输入的第一选择全部翻转：24 / 24。说明这段参数变化已经进入决策过程。', 'After removing the accumulated SD-LoRA change, the top choice flipped on all 24 fixed inputs: 24 / 24. The parameter change is already affecting decisions.')}</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="taskvector-paper"><strong>{t('参考与证据', 'Reference and evidence')}</strong><a href={taskArithmeticHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><ExternalBrandMark href={taskArithmeticHref} />Task Arithmetic ↗</a><span>{t('论文提供“把微调前后参数差看成方向”的背景；OpenEVO 的 24 / 24 行为干预来自我们自己的参数机制实验。', 'The paper motivates treating before/after parameter differences as directions; the 24 / 24 behavior intervention comes from our own OpenEVO mechanism experiment.')}</span></p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={measurementPackHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><ExternalBrandMark href={measurementPackHref} /> PR #317 · {t('参数行为干预证据', 'parameter behavior intervention')}</a> · <a href={technicalHref}>{t('完整 TaskVector 推导', 'full TaskVector derivation')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">14 / 23</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="m1a-identifiability" class="briefing-slide tone-gold" aria-labelledby="m1a-title">
    <div class="slide-inner m1a-slide">
      <h2 id="m1a-title">{t('第一次量“末段参数方向”时，75% 和 100% 其实是同一个模型状态', 'Our first late-direction measurement used the same model state for 75% and 100%')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('这是一次值得保留的科研自我修正。原 M1-A 按训练进度取 25% / 50% / 75% / 100% 四个锚点，但真正解析到保存下来的已接受参数状态时，它们是 R27 / R49 / R49 / R49。R14、R27、R49 这类编号表示训练过程中保存下来的不同参数状态。', 'This is an important scientific self-correction. The original M1-A chose 25% / 50% / 75% / 100% progress anchors, but the saved accepted parameter states resolved to R27 / R49 / R49 / R49. Labels such as R14, R27, and R49 denote distinct saved parameter states from training.')}</p>
      <div class="m1a-grid">
        <article class="m1a-old"><span>{t('原设计', 'original design')}</span><strong>75% = 100% = R49</strong><p>{t('最后两个“测量点”其实是同一份参数，所以 θ₁₀₀% − θ₇₅% = 0。这个 0 说明实验没有能力分辨最后一段方向。', 'The last two measurement points are the same parameters, so θ₁₀₀% − θ₇₅% = 0. That zero means the design cannot distinguish the final direction segment.')}</p></article>
        <article class="m1a-fix"><span>{t('修订取点', 'corrected anchors')}</span><strong>R14 → R27 → R49</strong><p>{t('后续修订实验改用相邻、而且确实不同的已接受参数状态，先保证每个测量点真的是不同模型。', 'The follow-up experiment uses adjacent, genuinely different accepted parameter states so each measurement point represents a genuinely different model.')}</p></article>
        <article class="m1a-result"><span>{t('恢复可辨识性', 'identifiability restored')}</span><strong>‖θ<sub>R49</sub> − θ<sub>R27</sub>‖ = 0.6082257746</strong><p>{t('末段向量严格非零，因此这个方向现在可以被测量。它只修复“能不能量”的问题；任务能力有没有提高仍要靠 WebShop 行为与冻结评测。', 'The late vector is strictly non-zero, so the direction is now measurable. This repairs the measurement question only; WebShop behavior and frozen evaluation still determine capability.')}</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="m1a-boundary"><strong>{t('我们改掉的判断', 'What changed in our judgment')}</strong>{t('看到零向量时，先检查两个端点是否真的是不同状态。这里原实验只能说明：两个端点其实一样，所以最后一段方向根本量不出来。“参数最后没有变化”这个结论没有证据支持。', 'When a vector is zero, first verify that its endpoints are genuinely different states. The original setup could not distinguish the final direction because its two endpoints were actually the same; it did not support a causal conclusion that the parameters stopped changing.')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={m1aPr350Href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><ExternalBrandMark href={m1aPr350Href} /> PR #350 · {t('原 M1-A 两个端点其实相同', 'original M1-A non-identifiability')}</a> · <a href={m1aPr358Href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><ExternalBrandMark href={m1aPr358Href} /> PR #358 · {t('改用相邻且不同的参数状态', 'distinct-state successor')}</a> · <a href={technicalHref}>{t('完整几何证据', 'full geometry')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">15 / 23</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="gdr" class="briefing-slide tone-rose" aria-labelledby="gdr-title">
    <div class="slide-inner">
      <h2 id="gdr-title">{t('我们当时叫它 GDR-v1，但真正跑的是“候选更新放不放行”', 'We called it GDR-v1, but what actually ran was candidate admission')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('本地 GDR-v1 的名字来自 Gated Delta Rule，但实现层级不同：我们先把 SD-LoRA candidate 训练出来，再做固定 16 题小测，决定 candidate 要不要进入下一轮；杨松霖原始 Gated Delta Rule 则直接定义 recurrent state 怎样读旧内容、算 residual、再按 β 写回。两者不能再用同一个“GDR”概念混讲。', 'Local GDR-v1 took its name from Gated Delta Rule, but it operates at a different level: we first train an SD-LoRA candidate, then use a fixed 16-task check to decide whether that candidate enters the next round. Songlin Yang’s original Gated Delta Rule instead directly defines how a recurrent state reads prior content, forms a residual, and writes it back with β. The two should not be conflated under one GDR concept.')}</p>
      <div class="before-after gdr-flow">
        <div class="before"><span>{t('论文里的原始机制', 'original paper mechanism')}</span><strong>{t('recurrent state：读旧值 → 算 residual → β 写回', 'recurrent state: read → residual → β write-back')}</strong><p>{t('原始 Gated Delta Rule 的 k、v、β、g 来自当前输入 / hidden representation；已有 state 参与 residual。candidate 训练完成后的外部 PASS / FAIL 小测属于我们本地 GDR-v1，处在另一层。', 'In the original Gated Delta Rule, k, v, β and g come from the current input / hidden representation, while the existing state participates through the residual. The external PASS / FAIL check after candidate training belongs to our local GDR-v1 at a different layer.')}</p><a href={gatedDeltaPaperHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><ExternalBrandMark href={gatedDeltaPaperHref} />Gated Delta Networks ↗</a></div>
        <div class="after"><span>{t('我们真正跑的 GDR-v1', 'our actual GDR-v1')}</span><strong>{t('当前模型 + 训练好的候选更新 → 固定 16 题小测 → 用不用这次更新', 'current model + trained candidate update → fixed 16-task check → use it or not')}</strong><p>{t('本地规则只做一件事：比较当前模型和“加上这次更新后的模型”在固定 16 题上的短期表现，然后决定这次更新要不要带到下一轮。', 'Our local rule does one thing: compare the current model with the model after the candidate update on a fixed 16-task check, then decide whether to carry that update into the next round.')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="gdr-why-gate"><strong>{t('为什么还要多做一次小测？', 'Why use a gate version?')}</strong>{t('当时我们还不知道该改哪一段参数、该改多少，所以先用了一个保守办法：候选更新先训练好，再看固定 16 题的小测结果，决定要不要用。新的问题也随之出现：一次很短的小测，会不会过早拒绝那些短期不够好、但长期可能有用的更新？', 'At the time, we did not know which parameter change would be useful long term, so we used a conservative shortcut: train the update, then let a short 16-task check decide whether to use it. That creates a new question: could a short check reject an update that looks weak now but would help later?')}</p>
      <p class="bottom-claim">{t('因此我们把两个计数分开看：OpenEVO 训练出了多少个 SD-LoRA 候选，以及 GDR 最终让多少个候选真正更新到后续模型。下一页就是 1.7B 正式线的实际结果。', 'We therefore track two counts separately: how many SD-LoRA candidates OpenEVO trained, and how many GDR allowed to update later model states. The next slide shows the formal 1.7B result.')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('GDR-v1 到底怎么筛选候选更新', 'Full GDR decision logic and experiment definition')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">16 / 23</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="one-seven-b" class="briefing-slide tone-green" aria-labelledby="one-seven-b-title">
    <div class="slide-inner dynamics-slide experiment-dynamics">
      <h2 id="one-seven-b-title">{t('训练产生了 44 个参数候选，GDR 只让 7 个进入后续模型', 'In the 1.7B experiment, only 7 of 44 candidates entered later model states')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t(`160 轮 / 20,480 次任务都跑完了。每轮 Score 前 20 轮平均 ${earlyScoreMean17B.toFixed(2)}，最后 20 轮平均 ${lateScoreMean17B.toFixed(2)}。训练没有停；真正显眼的是参数更新机会出现了 44 次，而 GDR 最后拒绝了其中 37 次。`, `All 160 rounds / 20,480 attempts completed. Mean training-round Score moves from ${earlyScoreMean17B.toFixed(2)} over the first 20 rounds to ${lateScoreMean17B.toFixed(2)} over the last 20. Training did not stop; the striking fact is that 44 parameter-update opportunities were trained and GDR rejected 37 of them.`)}</p>
      <div class="dynamics-grid">
        <figure class="dynamics-chart score-chart">
          <figcaption>{t('训练过程中每轮 WebShop Score', 'WebShop Score during training')} <span>{t('底部短线=候选；绿色粗线=GDR 接受', 'bottom ticks=candidates; thick green=GDR accepted')}</span></figcaption>
